  "whatChangedFrom002": [
    "Texture source: four seamless 512 px tiles were cut from the Codex art (volcano_side_0/1/2, volcano_duck_0; windows chosen automatically to be fully opaque, glow-free and at mid luminance) and box/triplanar-projected onto the 002 meshes, each tile twice with different orientations and mixed by soft masks so no aligned repeat shows.",
    "Shading: smooth normals with sharp edges only above 45 degrees; baked key light from the part-local upper left with a warm lit side and a cool purple shadow side, soft AO, a thin warm rim on upper convex edges and a thin smooth dark contour in the folds. No flat low-poly facets, no procedural noise, no dark slashes.",
    "Colour: every part is normalised to the 2D art values; all 22 baked objects have an average inside #4e3433..#5a3e3c (walls #53393b-#54393b) and a 90th-percentile highlight below #9a6058 (walls #7d5651-#855b55).",
    "Glow: thin curved emissive cracks only below ~0.9 m (2.3 % of the main atlas; every wall <= 4.8 %), gate seam and cave depth as in 002.",
    "Previews: same camera and lighting as 002; player_view has the three Codex billboards (jump, side, duck); compare_002_003.png and closeup_match.png added."
  ],
  "deviations": [
    "The control.py API still only produces whole scenes; the pipeline was run unchanged into runs/spellduel-volcano-kit-003 for the run record, the tiles and the bake come from the two scripts in the job folder. No generator source was modified.",
    "Texel density on the walls is 83-93 texels/m, a little under the requested 100-150: one 4096 atlas is shared by 13 walls, 2 gates and the cave. The backdrop rocks sit on a separate 2048 atlas at 25-32 texels/m (meant for 20-40 m).",
    "The two albedo atlases are shipped as JPEG (quality 92, 4:4:4) because the 4096 PNG alone is 16 MB, above the 15 MB kit budget; emissive mask and rock tiles are PNG.",
    "The painted facets are 2.4x larger than in the 2D obstacles (tile crops are 0.37-0.75 m, scaled to 0.9-1.8 m) so the repeat does not read on 4-6 m walls; brush strokes are therefore slightly larger than on the billboards.",
    "Hue match comes from the 2D art itself; the lit/shadow tints and the rim are baked, so instances rotated 180 degrees show the cool side toward the player (use Unlit to avoid double lighting).",
    "wall_straight_d and cave_entrance_a have one triangle fewer than 002 (degenerate triangle dropped in the FBX round trip); bounds are identical.",
    "Import verified only through the identical 001 exporter settings in a throwaway Unity 2022.3 project, not inside SpellDuel; mobile frame rate not measured."
  ],
